WEBVTT

00:00:00.212 --> 00:00:04.636
Chapter 1 Smile, please.

00:00:04.696 --> 00:00:11.422
Kit Chippans sat down on the harbour wall and looked across the bay.

00:00:11.482 --> 00:00:16.786
The sun was hot, and there wasn't a cloud in the sky.

00:00:16.846 --> 00:00:20.398
But Kit wasn't happy.

00:00:20.458 --> 00:00:25.882
There aren't any tourists this morning, he thought.

00:00:25.943 --> 00:00:29.492
I'm not going to earn much money today.

00:00:29.552 --> 00:00:38.421
The weather information on the radio said rain, and tourists always listen to weather information.

00:00:38.481 --> 00:00:40.682
But it was wrong.

00:00:40.742 --> 00:00:43.474
It isn't raining.

00:00:43.534 --> 00:00:48.385
Kit looked at the old camera in his hand.

00:00:48.445 --> 00:00:51.466
It belonged to his father.

00:00:51.526 --> 00:00:56.423
Kit wanted to earn money to buy a new camera.

00:00:56.483 --> 00:01:02.700
In the school holidays, he took photographs of the visitors to his town.

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:05.741
He loved taking photos.

00:01:05.801 --> 00:01:08.772
The tourists liked Kit.

00:01:08.832 --> 00:01:14.374
He smiled a lot, and he took good photographs of them.

00:01:14.434 --> 00:01:18.295
Kit's town was on a pretty bay.

00:01:18.355 --> 00:01:27.151
Some people there earned money from fishing, and some people worked in the small hotels beside the bay.

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:30.826
Rich people came there on holiday.

00:01:30.886 --> 00:01:37.181
They liked to sail yachts between the small islands across the bay.

00:01:37.241 --> 00:01:41.515
Kit looked at summer cloud.

00:01:41.575 --> 00:01:48.251
It was the biggest yacht in the harbour and it belonged to Bob Chapman.

00:01:48.311 --> 00:01:53.788
Bob's clients were always rich and famous people.

00:01:53.848 --> 00:01:58.362
Who has hired Bob Chapman's yacht today?

00:01:58.422 --> 00:02:00.172
Kit thought.

00:02:00.232 --> 00:02:02.743
Well, I know one thing.

00:02:02.803 --> 00:02:05.894
He won't give me any information.

00:02:05.954 --> 00:02:08.214
He never does.

00:02:08.274 --> 00:02:11.335
Kit was right.

00:02:11.395 --> 00:02:15.936
Bob Chapman promised his famous clients three things.

00:02:15.996 --> 00:02:23.130
Good sailing, good food, and no paparazzi.

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:30.615
In a house on a hill above the bay, Anna Lee was unhappy too.

00:02:30.674 --> 00:02:34.606
What am I going to do at home, Mom?

00:02:34.666 --> 00:02:40.778
She said, I'm 15, and I haven't got a holiday job.

00:02:40.838 --> 00:02:44.380
And all my friends are away.

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:48.421
That's not a problem, said her mother.

00:02:48.481 --> 00:02:51.286
You can clean the house for me.

00:02:51.346 --> 00:02:56.261
I don't like cleaning very much," said Anna.

00:02:56.321 --> 00:02:58.912
Can I do the cooking?

00:02:58.972 --> 00:03:04.103
The phone rang, and Anna's mother went to answer it.

00:03:04.163 --> 00:03:06.614
It was Bob Chapman.

00:03:06.674 --> 00:03:12.215
He was a friend of the family, and he wanted to speak to Anna.

00:03:12.275 --> 00:03:14.376
Hello, Anna!

00:03:14.436 --> 00:03:15.946
said Bob.

00:03:16.006 --> 00:03:19.925
What are you doing for the next three days?

00:03:19.985 --> 00:03:24.186
Uh, not much, said Anna.

00:03:24.246 --> 00:03:25.948
Why Bob?

00:03:26.008 --> 00:03:28.440
I've got a problem.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:33.204
Some clients want to sail to Moon Island tomorrow.

00:03:33.264 --> 00:03:37.948
I really want to do this job, and I've promised them.

00:03:38.008 --> 00:03:40.100
But Lily is ill.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:43.223
She cooks and cleans for me.

00:03:43.283 --> 00:03:45.404
Can you help Anna?

00:03:45.464 --> 00:03:48.132
You're good at cooking, aren't you?

00:03:48.192 --> 00:03:51.959
You cooked a great meal for your mother's birthday.

00:03:52.018 --> 00:03:54.750
You'll only have to cook one meal.

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:55.981
Lunch.

00:03:56.041 --> 00:03:58.802
We'll have dinner on the island.

00:03:58.862 --> 00:04:01.684
Yes, said Anna.

00:04:01.744 --> 00:04:04.866
Well, I'll have to ask mum.

00:04:04.926 --> 00:04:07.968
But yes, I'd like to.

00:04:08.028 --> 00:04:10.068
I'm a good cook.

00:04:10.128 --> 00:04:12.460
Who are your clients?

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:16.462
I can't tell you yet, said Bob.

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:18.023
You know why.

00:04:18.083 --> 00:04:22.316
I promised my clients no paparazzi.

00:04:22.376 --> 00:04:24.598
Can you come today, Anna?

00:04:24.657 --> 00:04:27.480
They want to leave early in the morning.

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:35.376
You'll have to clean the cabins and make the beds this afternoon and do some shopping for me.

00:04:35.436 --> 00:04:37.037
Is that okay?

00:04:37.096 --> 00:04:39.798
Okay, said Anna.

00:04:39.858 --> 00:04:43.422
I'll ask Mum to drive me down to the harbour.

00:04:43.482 --> 00:04:45.223
Thank you, Bob.

00:04:45.283 --> 00:04:47.444
I'll see you later.

00:04:47.504 --> 00:04:52.774
Anna put down the phone and talked to her mother about the job.

00:04:52.834 --> 00:04:56.046
I'll work hard, she said.

00:04:56.106 --> 00:05:01.218
Maybe Bob will give me a job on his boat for the summer.

00:05:01.278 --> 00:05:07.649
It didn't rain, and some tourists came to the harbor in the afternoon.

00:05:07.709 --> 00:05:13.806
Smile please, said kid, and he took their photographs.

00:05:13.866 --> 00:05:20.734
From the deck of a black motorboat, a young woman watched kid.

00:05:20.794 --> 00:05:25.336
A photographer, she thought.

00:05:25.395 --> 00:05:30.448
Perhaps he'll know about that big yacht in a harbor.

00:05:30.508 --> 00:05:33.610
A car arrived at the harbor.

00:05:33.670 --> 00:05:37.622
The woman watched a girl with short hair get out.

00:05:37.682 --> 00:05:44.344
A man met the girl, took her bag and helped her into a small boat.

00:05:44.403 --> 00:05:49.404
He was tall with white hair, and he wore a life jacket.

00:05:49.464 --> 00:05:53.416
His face was brown from being in the sun.

00:05:53.476 --> 00:05:56.526
The girl put on a life jacket.

00:05:56.586 --> 00:06:01.908
Then the small boat made its way out to the big yacht.

00:06:01.968 --> 00:06:07.490
Tommy, the woman called, come here.

00:06:07.549 --> 00:06:12.204
A big, strong man came up onto the deck of the motorboat.

00:06:12.264 --> 00:06:16.480
He wore a large white hat and a jacket.

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:18.732
What do you want, Jade?

00:06:18.792 --> 00:06:20.464
He asked.

00:06:20.524 --> 00:06:27.588
The woman looked at Kit, then across the water at Anna on summer cloud.

00:06:27.648 --> 00:06:29.900
What do you think?

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:34.142
She asked, yes or no.

00:06:34.202 --> 00:06:36.784
Tommy understood.

00:06:36.844 --> 00:06:41.775
He touched his jacket, where he had a small gun.

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:44.244
He suddenly smiled.

00:06:44.304 --> 00:06:47.177
Yes, my dear.

00:06:47.236 --> 00:06:50.399
He answered.

00:06:50.459 --> 00:06:53.972
Track three.

00:06:54.032 --> 00:07:00.568
In a house on a hill above the bay, Anna Lee was unhappy too.

00:07:00.628 --> 00:07:04.562
What am I going to do at home, Mom?

00:07:04.621 --> 00:07:10.716
She said, I'm 15 and I haven't got a holiday job.

00:07:10.776 --> 00:07:14.306
And all my friends are away.

00:07:14.366 --> 00:07:18.359
That's not a problem, said her mother.

00:07:18.418 --> 00:07:20.619
You can clean the house for me.

00:07:20.639 --> 00:07:26.212
I don't like cleaning very much, said Anna.

00:07:26.272 --> 00:07:28.854
Can I do the cooking?

00:07:28.914 --> 00:07:34.046
The phone rang and Anna's mother went to answer it.

00:07:34.106 --> 00:07:36.557
It was Bob Chapman.

00:07:36.617 --> 00:07:38.982
He was a friend of the family.

00:07:39.042 --> 00:07:42.146
and he wanted to speak to Anna.

00:07:42.206 --> 00:07:45.868
Hello Anna, said Bob.

00:07:45.928 --> 00:07:50.338
What are you doing for the next three days?

00:07:50.398 --> 00:07:54.119
Not much, said Anna.

00:07:54.179 --> 00:07:55.870
Why Bob?

00:07:55.929 --> 00:07:58.370
I've got a problem.

00:07:58.430 --> 00:08:03.121
Some clients want to sail to Moon Island tomorrow.

00:08:03.181 --> 00:08:07.879
I really want to do this job and I've promised them.

00:08:07.938 --> 00:08:10.016
But Lily is ill.

00:08:10.076 --> 00:08:13.148
She cooks and cleans for me.

00:08:13.208 --> 00:08:15.310
Can you help Anna?

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:18.062
You're good at cooking, aren't you?

00:08:18.122 --> 00:08:21.906
You cooked a great meal for your mother's birthday.

00:08:21.966 --> 00:08:24.688
You'll only have to cook one meal.

00:08:24.748 --> 00:08:25.930
Lunch.

00:08:25.990 --> 00:08:30.263
We'll have dinner on the island.

00:08:30.323 --> 00:08:33.576
Chapter 2.

00:08:33.636 --> 00:08:39.064
Harbor Life Jade sat on the harbor wall.

00:08:39.124 --> 00:08:44.476
Kit saw her, held up his camera and said, Smile please.

00:08:44.536 --> 00:08:46.607
Jade didn't smile.

00:08:46.667 --> 00:08:50.308
No, please don't take my photo.

00:08:50.368 --> 00:08:51.818
She said.

00:08:51.878 --> 00:08:55.350
Then she stood up and put out her hand.

00:08:55.410 --> 00:08:56.860
Hello.

00:08:56.920 --> 00:09:04.137
My name is Jade and I work for a new magazine, Harbor Life.

00:09:04.197 --> 00:09:08.474
and I'm looking for photographs of famous people.

00:09:08.534 --> 00:09:13.726
We want to write a story about famous visitors to this harbor.

00:09:13.786 --> 00:09:17.460
I've seen you take a lot of photographs.

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:19.340
Are they good?

00:09:19.401 --> 00:09:22.082
Yes, said Kit.

00:09:22.142 --> 00:09:25.304
He smiled and shook Jade's hand.

00:09:25.364 --> 00:09:30.908
My name's Kit Jipan and I work here in the school holidays.

00:09:30.968 --> 00:09:34.626
I want to earn money to buy a better camera.

00:09:34.686 --> 00:09:38.134
Erm, are you staying in town?

00:09:38.195 --> 00:09:39.536
No.

00:09:39.596 --> 00:09:41.968
I arrived this morning.

00:09:42.028 --> 00:09:45.632
My boat's over there, said Jade.

00:09:45.692 --> 00:09:50.388
Then she looked across the harbour at Summer Cloud.

00:09:50.448 --> 00:09:54.420
That's a beautiful yacht out there, isn't it?

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:56.931
Who has hired it, Kit?

00:09:56.991 --> 00:10:05.685
Do you know, I'd like some photographs of its clients for my magazine and some information about them.

00:10:05.746 --> 00:10:10.168
You know, about their life, their work.

00:10:10.228 --> 00:10:13.520
Could you do that for me?

00:10:13.580 --> 00:10:16.150
Kit stopped smiling.

00:10:16.210 --> 00:10:18.800
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:23.122
But Bob Chapman doesn't give information about his clients.

00:10:23.182 --> 00:10:26.534
You can talk to his crew, can't you?

00:10:26.594 --> 00:10:28.135
Asked Jade.

00:10:28.195 --> 00:10:30.076
No, said Kit.

00:10:30.136 --> 00:10:32.368
I'm sorry, but I can't.

00:10:32.428 --> 00:10:34.459
Yes, you can.

00:10:34.519 --> 00:10:36.050
Said Jade.

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:38.052
I'll pay you well.

00:10:38.112 --> 00:10:41.154
Then you can buy your new camera.

00:10:41.214 --> 00:10:43.811
She smiled and waited.

00:10:43.871 --> 00:10:50.750
I do need a new camera, for kid, and I do want to be a photographer.

00:10:50.810 --> 00:10:53.720
And this woman is nice.

00:10:53.780 --> 00:10:55.842
Why not?

00:10:55.902 --> 00:10:59.262
I'll do it, he said.

00:10:59.322 --> 00:11:05.045
Okay, you're hired, said Jade.

00:11:05.105 --> 00:11:07.556
They shook hands again.

00:11:07.616 --> 00:11:10.057
Come to my boat tonight.

00:11:10.117 --> 00:11:13.700
Let's say, at six o'clock.

00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:18.893
I can't promise to get any photos of the clients," said Kit.

00:11:18.953 --> 00:11:20.574
That's okay.

00:11:20.634 --> 00:11:25.786
Try to get some information, and we can talk about it tonight.

00:11:25.846 --> 00:11:28.516
She walked back to the motorboat.

00:11:28.576 --> 00:11:31.167
Kit looked at his watch.

00:11:31.227 --> 00:11:33.328
It was four o'clock.

00:11:33.388 --> 00:11:38.260
I've only got two hours, he thought.

00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:41.812
Anna's mother called her.

00:11:41.872 --> 00:11:45.195
I can't talk, Mum," said Anna.

00:11:45.254 --> 00:11:47.636
Yes, I've cleaned the cabins.

00:11:47.696 --> 00:11:51.318
But I've got to do some shopping for tomorrow's lunch.

00:11:51.378 --> 00:11:55.762
And, oh, I haven't made the beds yet.

00:11:55.822 --> 00:11:57.332
Sorry, Mum.

00:11:57.392 --> 00:11:59.434
I've got to go.

00:11:59.493 --> 00:12:03.536
Bob was happy with Anna's hard work.

00:12:03.596 --> 00:12:06.339
It was a good time to tell her.

00:12:06.398 --> 00:12:07.619
Anna?

00:12:07.679 --> 00:12:08.850
He called.

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:11.123
Stop work and listen.

00:12:11.183 --> 00:12:14.666
Do you want to know the names of my clients?

00:12:14.726 --> 00:12:19.318
Yes, please," said Anna, and she sat down.

00:12:19.378 --> 00:12:22.339
Okay, said Bob.

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:25.491
They're famous film stars.

00:12:25.551 --> 00:12:28.872
They're making a new film on Moon Island.

00:12:28.932 --> 00:12:32.344
There's a big film crew on the island already.

00:12:32.404 --> 00:12:36.356
But Anna, you mustn't talk about it.

00:12:36.416 --> 00:12:38.616
I won't, said Anna.

00:12:38.676 --> 00:12:39.886
I promise.

00:12:39.946 --> 00:12:42.496
Tell me, please, Bob.

00:12:42.556 --> 00:12:44.258
Who are they?

00:12:44.318 --> 00:12:46.200
Bob smiled.

00:12:46.260 --> 00:12:52.824
Well, she likes diamond rings and the color green.

00:12:52.884 --> 00:13:01.791
And he's been in two films with her and Charles Ford and Maria Chilini.

00:13:01.851 --> 00:13:06.224
Anna got up and jumped up and down on the deck.

00:13:06.284 --> 00:13:09.777
Wow, Chaz and Chilini.

00:13:09.837 --> 00:13:12.238
They're in all the magazines.

00:13:12.298 --> 00:13:14.790
I read about them every week.

00:13:14.850 --> 00:13:20.304
She always wears diamond rings, and she always has white flowers in her room.

00:13:20.364 --> 00:13:24.816
And he white flowers, Bob said suddenly.

00:13:24.876 --> 00:13:29.680
Anna, can you go and buy some white flowers for her cabin?

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:33.432
Okay, I'll go now, said Anna.

00:13:33.492 --> 00:13:36.500
I've got to buy the fish as well.

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:41.339
Anna took the small boat back to the harbor wall.

00:13:41.399 --> 00:13:50.363
She went to the market, and five minutes later, she came out with her arms full of big white flowers.

00:13:50.424 --> 00:13:53.925
She stood in the sunshine and smelled them.

00:13:53.985 --> 00:13:57.927
She was the happiest girl in the world.

00:13:57.987 --> 00:14:01.538
I can tell all my friends at school.

00:14:01.598 --> 00:14:07.395
I've met Chas and Chilini, she thought.

00:14:07.455 --> 00:14:10.890
Kit held up his camera.

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:14.051
Smile please, he said to Anna.

00:14:14.111 --> 00:14:20.533
Hello, I'm taking photographs for a new magazine, Harbor Life.

00:14:20.593 --> 00:14:24.164
Aren't you young to be a magazine photographer?

00:14:24.224 --> 00:14:25.684
Anna asked.

00:14:25.744 --> 00:14:28.606
I'm 16, said Kit.

00:14:28.666 --> 00:14:30.676
It's my holiday job.

00:14:30.736 --> 00:14:34.007
I want to be a photographer when I leave school.

00:14:34.067 --> 00:14:36.841
But I need a better camera for that.

00:14:36.901 --> 00:14:39.164
Are you on holiday here?

00:14:39.224 --> 00:14:40.285
No.

00:14:40.345 --> 00:14:42.906
I live here, said Anna.

00:14:42.966 --> 00:14:45.796
I'm working on that big yacht over there.

00:14:45.856 --> 00:14:47.387
Some are cloud.

00:14:47.447 --> 00:14:49.807
It belongs to my mother's friend.

00:14:49.867 --> 00:14:52.028
Yes, Bob Chapman.

00:14:52.088 --> 00:14:54.759
I know him, said Kid.

00:14:54.819 --> 00:14:57.640
You know Bob, asked Anna.

00:14:57.700 --> 00:15:00.360
Yes, he's a good sailor.

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:02.211
One of the best.

00:15:02.271 --> 00:15:03.871
I'm Kid.

00:15:03.931 --> 00:15:05.682
What's your name?

00:15:05.742 --> 00:15:07.328
Anna.

00:15:07.388 --> 00:15:10.056
Who were the flowers for, Anna?

00:15:10.116 --> 00:15:16.462
Uh, therefore one of the cabins, Anna said carefully.

00:15:16.522 --> 00:15:21.006
Anna and Kit sat down on the harbor wall.

00:15:21.066 --> 00:15:26.000
They talked and watched the fishing boats along the harbor wall.

00:15:26.060 --> 00:15:29.102
People stopped to buy fish.

00:15:29.162 --> 00:15:31.394
And what about you, Anna?

00:15:31.454 --> 00:15:32.996
Ask Kit.

00:15:33.056 --> 00:15:36.332
Aren't you young to be working on a boat?

00:15:36.392 --> 00:15:41.528
Oh, it's a holiday job for me too, said Anna.

00:15:41.588 --> 00:15:50.630
But it's the best holiday job in the world, Chas, and she suddenly stopped speaking and looked down.

00:15:50.690 --> 00:15:55.612
Who, said Kit, Anna thought quickly.

00:15:55.672 --> 00:15:59.872
Chapman, Bob Chapman, she said.

00:15:59.932 --> 00:16:02.773
The yacht belongs to Bob Chapman.

00:16:02.833 --> 00:16:06.568
Yes, I know, said Kit.

00:16:06.628 --> 00:16:09.153
Anna looked at her watch.

00:16:09.213 --> 00:16:10.824
I'm sorry, Kit.

00:16:10.884 --> 00:16:12.214
I must go.

00:16:12.274 --> 00:16:17.056
I've got to take these flowers to the yacht and get some fish.

00:16:17.116 --> 00:16:19.968
She stood up and walked away.

00:16:20.028 --> 00:16:22.168
Her face was hot.

00:16:22.228 --> 00:16:23.789
Oh, no.

00:16:23.849 --> 00:16:26.850
Did he hear Chaz's name?

00:16:26.910 --> 00:16:33.613
From the harbor wall, Kit watched Anna buy some fish from one of the fishing boats.

00:16:33.672 --> 00:16:40.875
Then with a bag of fish and the white flowers in her arms, she got into a small boat.

00:16:40.935 --> 00:16:43.296
Kit smiled.

00:16:43.356 --> 00:16:45.457
It was easy.

00:16:45.517 --> 00:16:50.810
He always read stories about famous film stars in magazines.

00:16:50.870 --> 00:16:55.402
He wanted to take photographs for those magazines one day.

00:16:55.462 --> 00:16:57.952
He remembered one story.

00:16:58.012 --> 00:17:03.964
Chas Ford and Maria Chilini were going to make a new film.

00:17:04.024 --> 00:17:10.596
He couldn't remember the name of it, but there was an island in the story.

00:17:10.656 --> 00:17:14.548
Was it one of the islands across the bay?

00:17:14.608 --> 00:17:22.532
Kit watched Anna take the small boats out to Summer Cloud with the white flowers beside her.

00:17:22.592 --> 00:17:27.465
And then he remembered another story about Maria Chilini.

00:17:27.525 --> 00:17:31.647
She loved white flowers.

00:17:31.707 --> 00:17:33.866
It's then.

00:17:33.926 --> 00:17:37.056
It's Chas and Chilini.

00:17:37.116 --> 00:17:41.830
I've got some information now, kid thought.

00:17:41.890 --> 00:17:46.633
I can tell Jade at six o'clock.

00:17:46.693 --> 00:17:50.206
Chapter three.

00:17:50.266 --> 00:17:54.768
Lies and more lies.

00:17:54.828 --> 00:18:00.242
It was morning and summer cloud was at sea.

00:18:00.302 --> 00:18:04.038
Anna couldn't see the harbour or the town.

00:18:04.098 --> 00:18:08.462
The sun shone, and the sea was calm.

00:18:08.522 --> 00:18:13.154
It's nice and quiet out here, she thought.

00:18:13.214 --> 00:18:16.746
But Bob Chapman wasn't happy.

00:18:16.807 --> 00:18:21.818
We need more wind in the sails, he said to Anna.

00:18:21.878 --> 00:18:24.760
We need to go faster.

00:18:24.820 --> 00:18:32.410
Anna looked up at the white sails, the big main sail and the sail at the front.

00:18:32.470 --> 00:18:35.089
Can't you switch the engine on?"

00:18:35.149 --> 00:18:36.470
she asked.

00:18:36.530 --> 00:18:38.970
I don't want to switch it on yet.

00:18:39.030 --> 00:18:40.511
replied Bob.

00:18:40.571 --> 00:18:43.332
The engine makes a lot of noise.

00:18:43.392 --> 00:18:46.514
I don't think Chaz will like that.

00:18:46.574 --> 00:18:48.595
How is he now?

00:18:48.655 --> 00:18:50.916
I'll go down and see.

00:18:50.976 --> 00:18:52.816
said Anna.

00:18:52.876 --> 00:18:59.470
In his cabin, Chaz Ford lay on the bed with his eyes closed.

00:18:59.530 --> 00:19:03.188
He wanted to be back on land.

00:19:03.249 --> 00:19:10.168
Anna gave him a glass of water and said, drink this, Mr. Ford.

00:19:10.228 --> 00:19:16.649
He drank it, and then said, I really don't feel well, Anna.

00:19:16.709 --> 00:19:22.250
This is the first time I've sailed on a yacht, and I don't like it.

00:19:22.310 --> 00:19:25.862
When will we arrive at Moon Island?

00:19:25.922 --> 00:19:32.152
At the end of the day, Anna told him, you'll feel better soon.

00:19:32.212 --> 00:19:40.056
She went back up onto the deck and thought, shall I tell all my friends at school about this?

00:19:40.116 --> 00:19:45.650
At 10 o'clock, Maria Chilini came up onto the deck.

00:19:45.710 --> 00:19:51.904
She was beautiful, just like her pictures in the magazines.

00:19:51.964 --> 00:19:58.110
Her hair was long and red and her eyes were green.

00:19:58.170 --> 00:20:01.362
Her swimsuit was green too.

00:20:01.422 --> 00:20:05.634
Her diamond rings shone in the sunshine.

00:20:05.694 --> 00:20:12.435
She smiled at Anna and said, Those white flowers in my cabin are beautiful.

00:20:12.495 --> 00:20:14.526
Did you put them there?

00:20:14.586 --> 00:20:18.346
Yes, Miss Chilini replied Anna.

00:20:18.406 --> 00:20:20.057
Thank you.

00:20:20.117 --> 00:20:22.867
And call me Maria.

00:20:22.927 --> 00:20:28.798
She sat on the deck and said, Come and talk to me Anna.

00:20:28.858 --> 00:20:32.060
Anna sat down beside her.

00:20:32.120 --> 00:20:35.274
It's nice out here, isn't it?

00:20:35.334 --> 00:20:37.936
Maria, she asked.

00:20:37.996 --> 00:20:41.339
Oh, it's beautiful, said Maria.

00:20:41.400 --> 00:20:44.452
Beautiful and quiet.

00:20:44.512 --> 00:20:47.776
Do you like being famous, Maria?

00:20:47.836 --> 00:20:49.648
Yes, I do.

00:20:49.708 --> 00:20:53.190
But the paparazzi can be a big problem.

00:20:53.250 --> 00:20:58.388
They always want photos, photos, photos.

00:20:58.448 --> 00:21:02.272
When did you first want to be a film star?"

00:21:02.332 --> 00:21:03.872
asked Anna.

00:21:03.933 --> 00:21:11.116
Oh, I was only a little girl, about nine or ten years old.

00:21:11.176 --> 00:21:14.127
My father wasn't happy about it.

00:21:14.188 --> 00:21:20.130
He wanted me to be a doctor, but he understands now.

00:21:20.190 --> 00:21:24.463
Anna and Maria talked for a long time.

00:21:24.523 --> 00:21:28.800
She's really nice, thought Anna.

00:21:28.860 --> 00:21:39.096
The sun was high in the sky now, and Anna stood up and said, I'm sorry Maria, I've got to go and cook the lunch.

00:21:39.156 --> 00:21:41.006
What are you cooking?

00:21:41.066 --> 00:21:42.717
Maria asked.

00:21:42.777 --> 00:21:45.637
Fish, replied Anna.

00:21:45.697 --> 00:21:50.318
Oh, I love fish, smart Maria.

00:21:50.378 --> 00:21:53.929
And she lay back in the sunshine.

00:21:53.989 --> 00:21:57.440
Kit opened his eyes.

00:21:57.500 --> 00:21:59.272
It was dark.

00:21:59.332 --> 00:22:02.608
He could hear the sound of an engine.

00:22:02.668 --> 00:22:05.940
Then he heard the sound of seabirds.

00:22:06.000 --> 00:22:11.704
He stood up, found a light switch and switched on the light.

00:22:11.764 --> 00:22:18.880
He was in a small cabin without a window and it moved from side to side.

00:22:18.940 --> 00:22:24.005
I'm on a boat and it's moving.

00:22:24.065 --> 00:22:27.107
What am I doing here?

00:22:27.167 --> 00:22:29.672
He looked at his watch.

00:22:29.732 --> 00:22:33.695
It was three o'clock in the afternoon.

00:22:33.755 --> 00:22:37.456
He tried to remember the night before.

00:22:37.516 --> 00:22:39.376
Yes.

00:22:39.436 --> 00:22:43.208
I went to the motorboat at six o'clock.

00:22:43.268 --> 00:22:51.780
I told Jade and Tommy about Chas Ford and Maria Chilini, and they were nice to me.

00:22:51.840 --> 00:22:54.991
They liked my photos of the harbour.

00:22:55.051 --> 00:22:57.452
Pem, what happened?

00:22:57.512 --> 00:23:00.620
I can't remember.

00:23:00.680 --> 00:23:04.739
He sat down and thought hard.

00:23:04.799 --> 00:23:08.820
Yes, that's it.

00:23:08.880 --> 00:23:12.702
I wanted to leave and I got up.

00:23:12.762 --> 00:23:15.623
And what was it?

00:23:15.683 --> 00:23:17.614
A drink.

00:23:17.674 --> 00:23:21.295
Jade gave me a drink.

00:23:21.355 --> 00:23:24.726
It had a nasty taste.

00:23:24.787 --> 00:23:29.730
Kit switched on his mobile phone to call his father.

00:23:29.790 --> 00:23:33.004
But his phone didn't work.

00:23:33.064 --> 00:23:37.856
I trusted Jade and Tommy, he thought.

00:23:37.916 --> 00:23:41.547
But I don't really know them.

00:23:41.607 --> 00:23:48.300
Kit opened the door of the cabin and ran angrily up the stairs.

00:23:48.360 --> 00:23:51.762
He was on the deck of the black motorboat.

00:23:51.822 --> 00:23:55.133
The sun shone in a blue sky.

00:23:55.193 --> 00:23:59.375
Tommy was at the steering wheel with Jade beside him.

00:23:59.435 --> 00:24:07.819
Kit couldn't see any land, but he could see the sails of summer cloud a long way in front of them.

00:24:07.879 --> 00:24:11.501
Now he was angry and worried.

00:24:11.561 --> 00:24:14.102
Why did I trust them?

00:24:14.163 --> 00:24:16.244
He thought.

00:24:16.304 --> 00:24:18.364
Tommy!

00:24:18.424 --> 00:24:19.645
Jade!

00:24:19.705 --> 00:24:21.116
He shouted.

00:24:21.176 --> 00:24:23.007
What's happening?

00:24:23.067 --> 00:24:25.263
Where are we going?

00:24:25.323 --> 00:24:29.730
Jade turned and said, hello, Kit.

00:24:29.790 --> 00:24:31.961
Do you want some lunch?

00:24:32.021 --> 00:24:33.672
No thanks.

00:24:33.732 --> 00:24:35.503
Reply, Kit.

00:24:35.563 --> 00:24:38.614
Why am I here on your motorboat?

00:24:38.674 --> 00:24:41.486
My father will be very worried.

00:24:41.546 --> 00:24:43.447
Jade smiled.

00:24:43.507 --> 00:24:45.438
You went to sleep.

00:24:45.498 --> 00:24:50.480
I tried to stop you, but you were very tired.

00:24:50.540 --> 00:24:53.202
You can call your father now.

00:24:53.262 --> 00:24:55.893
Tell him about your new job.

00:24:55.953 --> 00:25:00.286
My mobile doesn't work here, said Kit.

00:25:00.346 --> 00:25:02.057
I'm what job?

00:25:02.117 --> 00:25:06.050
I've already told you about Chaz and Chilini.

00:25:06.110 --> 00:25:09.842
Why are we following Bob Chapman's yacht?

00:25:09.902 --> 00:25:15.708
Jade held the steering wheel and Tommy came to talk to Kit.

00:25:15.768 --> 00:25:18.860
You're a good photographer, Kit.

00:25:18.920 --> 00:25:20.270
He said.

00:25:20.330 --> 00:25:25.206
We just want you to take some photographs of Maria and Chaz.

00:25:25.266 --> 00:25:27.450
for the magazine.

00:25:27.510 --> 00:25:29.060
No.

00:25:29.120 --> 00:25:33.094
Don't be silly, Kit," said Tommy.

00:25:33.154 --> 00:25:35.266
Think about the money.

00:25:35.326 --> 00:25:39.048
Don't you want to buy your new camera?

00:25:39.108 --> 00:25:42.460
Kit looked at Jade and Tommy.

00:25:42.520 --> 00:25:45.924
Their faces looked hard in the sunlight.

00:25:45.984 --> 00:25:49.226
He really didn't trust them now.

00:25:49.287 --> 00:25:54.681
He remembered Anna's happy face and remembered her words.

00:25:54.741 --> 00:25:59.175
It's the best holiday job in the world.

00:25:59.235 --> 00:26:04.140
Bob Chapman doesn't like paparazzi, said kid.

00:26:04.200 --> 00:26:07.082
He'll just sail away from you.

00:26:07.142 --> 00:26:10.584
No, he won't, said Tommy.

00:26:10.644 --> 00:26:13.187
He won't have time.

00:26:13.247 --> 00:26:19.892
Well, I won't take any photographs for you, kid told them.

00:26:19.952 --> 00:26:22.234
Take me back to the harbor.

00:26:22.294 --> 00:26:23.814
Now.

00:26:23.875 --> 00:26:29.618
but Tommy and Jade just smiled.

00:26:29.678 --> 00:26:38.854
Track 4 At 10 o'clock, Maria Chilini came up onto the deck.

00:26:38.914 --> 00:26:45.117
She was beautiful, just like her pictures in the magazines.

00:26:45.178 --> 00:26:51.322
Her hair was long and red and her eyes were green.

00:26:51.382 --> 00:26:54.544
Her swimsuit was green too.

00:26:54.604 --> 00:26:58.848
Her diamond rings shone in the sunshine.

00:26:58.908 --> 00:27:05.663
She smiled at Anna and said, Those white flowers in my cabin are beautiful.

00:27:05.723 --> 00:27:07.744
Did you put them there?

00:27:07.804 --> 00:27:11.567
Yes, Miss Chilini, replied Anna.

00:27:11.628 --> 00:27:13.278
Thank you.

00:27:13.338 --> 00:27:16.090
And call me Maria.

00:27:16.150 --> 00:27:22.025
She sat on the deck and said, Come and talk to me Anna.

00:27:22.085 --> 00:27:25.288
